=== (4) the tournament bridge: AP = self-complementary fixed point of LRC Z_2 ===
  SC tournaments = fixed points of complement (T=T^op up to iso), have -1 anti-aut (THM-024).
  AP {1..12} = fixed set of sigma:i->-i in (Z/13)*, tight at the roots of unity.
  Both: the order-2 element of the governing group pins the extremal/fixed configuration.

VERDICT: if all tight = sigma-invariant AND asymmetric lifts are systematically looser
=> sigma-invariance (LRC self-complementarity) is a genuine tight-locus condition,
the same Z_2 that governs the tournament SC structure -- one involution, two halves.
